<section id="A6.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">F.2 </span>Composite Tags</h3>

<div id="A6.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A6.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><a href="#A6.F15" title="Figure 15 ‣ F.3 Qualitative Analysis ‣ Appendix F System 2: COT-augmented Admissions ‣ ‘Rich Dad, Poor Lad’: How do Large Language Models Contextualize Socioeconomic Factors in College Admission ?" class="ltx_ref ltx_refmacro_autoref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Figure 15</span></a>shows the complementary trends in composite tags to <a href="#S5.F6" title="Figure 6 ‣ LLMs exhibit clear asymmetries in how they weigh SES and academic factors across contexts. ‣ 5.3.2 Reasoning Patterns by SES and Decision ‣ 5.3 SES vs Academic Factors in Deliberation ‣ 5 System 2: COT-augmented Admission ‣ ‘Rich Dad, Poor Lad’: How do Large Language Models Contextualize Socioeconomic Factors in College Admission ?" class="ltx_ref ltx_refmacro_autoref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Figure 6</span></a> for rejected and admitted applicants.</p>
